-- title:
--   Separability of the full modular function field over L(j)
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure and let $N$ be a nonzero natural number. Write $jq \in \mathbb{Q}((q))$ for the Laurent series $q^{-1}$ times the power series `jNumQ` obtained from `jNum` by coefficientwise reduction into $\mathbb{Q}$, and let `modularFunctionFieldFull N` be the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the set `divisorExpansions N`, i.e. by the elements `qExpand ℚ d jq` for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $N$. Let `coeffEmb L` be the ring homomorphism $\mathbb{Q}((q)) \to L((q))$ applying $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ to each coefficient, and let $E =$ `laurentBaseChange L (modularFunctionFieldFull N)` be the intermediate field of $L((q))$ generated over $L$ by the image under `coeffEmb L` of `modularFunctionFieldFull N`. Since `coeffEmb L jq` lies in $E$, it determines an element of $E$, and one may form the intermediate field $X \subseteq E$ generated over $L$ by that single element. The assertion is `Algebra.IsSeparable X E`: every element of $E$ is integral over $X$ with separable minimal polynomial.
--
--   This is the separability of the covering of the $j$-line by the modular curve of level $N$, in the base-changed Laurent-series model with constant field $L$ and with the ground field taken to be the subfield generated by the single $q$-expansion of $j$. It is the hypothesis under which $dj$ generates the module of Kähler differentials of the modular function field, and it is used in the treatment of differentials and $q$-expansions on modular curves.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_isSeparable_adjoin_coeffEmb_jq_full.lean

